=== README.md ===
# sample-app

rocket web app generated by [rise](https://github.com/EryyynIT/rise).

Stack: rocket + sled (embedded — no database server).

## Prerequisites

- Rust — https://rustup.rs (`rise doctor` checks this machine)

## Run

```sh
cargo run
```

The server listens on http://localhost:3000.

## Test

```sh
cargo test
```

=== src/db.rs ===
//! Embedded key-value storage (sled).

use sled::Db;

/// Open the embedded database at `DB_PATH` (defaults to a local `data/`
/// directory, created on first run).
pub fn open() -> Result<Db, sled::Error> {
    let path = std::env::var("DB_PATH").unwrap_or_else(|_| "data".to_owned());
    sled::open(path)
}
=== src/main.rs ===
use rocket::routes;

mod db;

#[rocket::main]
async fn main() -> Result<(), rocket::Error> {
    // Loads .env when present (DATABASE_URL & co.); absent is fine.
    let _ = dotenvy::dotenv();
    let db = db::open().expect("failed to open the database");
    // Listen on 0.0.0.0:3000 like every other backend rise generates;
    // rocket's own defaults are 127.0.0.1:8000.
    let config = rocket::Config {
        address: std::net::Ipv4Addr::UNSPECIFIED.into(),
        port: 3000,
        ..Default::default()
    };
    let rocket = rocket::custom(config)
        .manage(db)
        .mount("/", routes![root]);

    println!("listening on http://localhost:3000");
    rocket.launch().await?;
    Ok(())
}

#[rocket::get("/")]
fn root() -> &'static str {
    "Hello from sample-app!"
}
